full_descriptions:
["AWD-007118-S4", "HETEROGENEOUS ADAPTIVELY PRODUCED PHOTONIC INTERFACES  (HAPPI)", "HETEROGENEOUS ADAPTIVELY PRODUCED PHOTONIC INTERFACES (HAPPI)", "MIT WILL PERFORM FUNDAMENTAL RESEARCH ON THE PROJECT. THE FREEFORM OPTICS DESIGN METHODOLOGY AND EXPERIMENTAL IMPLEMENTATION HAVE BEEN DISCLOSED IN PEER-REVIEWED PUBLICATIONS: PHOTON. RES. 12, 1055-1066 (2024); LASER PHOTONICS REV. 17, 2200025 (2023). THE HIGH-INDEX GLASS MATERIAL PREPARATION AND NANOIMPRINT FABRICATION TECHNOLOGY INVOLVED FOR THE MICRO-OPTICS FABRICATION HAVE ALSO BEEN PUBLICLY DISCLOSED IN: ADV. OPT. MATER. 2, 478-486 (2014); ADV. OPT. MATER. 2, 759-764 (2014). THEREFORE, THE MIT TASKS ARE FUNDAMENTAL RESEARCH IN NATURE.
SOW FOR GEORGIA TECH
MIT WILL PERFORM THE FOLLOWING TASKS DURING PHASE I OF THE PROJECT (04/2025 – 09/20", "MIT WILL PERFORM FUNDAMENTAL RESEARCH ON THE PROJECT. THE FREEFORM OPTICS DESIGN METHODOLOGY AND EXPERIMENTAL IMPLEMENTATION HAVE BEEN DISCLOSED IN PEER-REVIEWED PUBLICATIONS: PHOTON. RES. 12, 1055-1066 (2024); LASER PHOTONICS REV. 17, 2200025 (2023). THE HIGH-INDEX GLASS MATERIAL PREPARATION AND NANOIMPRINT FABRICATION TECHNOLOGY INVOLVED FOR THE MICRO-OPTICS FABRICATION HAVE ALSO BEEN PUBLICLY DISCLOSED IN: ADV. OPT. MATER. 2, 478-486 (2014); ADV. OPT. MATER. 2, 759-764 (2014). THEREFORE, THE MIT TASKS ARE FUNDAMENTAL RESEARCH IN NATURE.
SOW FOR GEORGIA TECH
MIT WILL PERFORM THE FOLLOWING TASKS DURING PHASE I OF THE PROJECT (04/2025 – 09/2026):
1. DESIGN OF THE MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLERS FOR EFFICIENT WAVEGUIDE COUPLING;
2. MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLER FABRICATION USING IN-HOUSE PROTOTYPING FACILITIES;
3. OPTICAL CHARACTERIZATION OF THE MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLERS;
4. PACKAGING AND ASSEMBLY OF THE MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLERS WITH PHOTONIC WAVEGUIDES.
MIT WILL PERFORM THE FOLLOWING TASKS DURING PHASE II OF THE PROJECT (10/2026 – 03/2028):
1. DESIGN OPTIMIZATION OF THE MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLERS FOR EFFICIENT WAVEGUIDE COUPLING BASED ON PHASE I OUTCOME;
2. DEMONSTRATION OF SCALABLE MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLER INTEGRATION WITH PICS FABRICATED VIA STANDARD PHOTONIC FOUNDRY SERVICE;
3. HIGH-THROUGHPUT OPTICAL CHARACTERIZATION OF LARGE MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLER ARRAYS;
4. PACKAGING AND ASSEMBLY OF THE MICRO-OPTICAL COUPLERS WITH PHOTONIC WAVEGUIDE CIRCUITS.", "THE HETEROGENEOUS ADAPTIVELY PRODUCED PHOTONIC INTERFACES (HAPPI) PROGRAM AIMS TO CREATE A 1000X INCREASE IN THE INFORMATION TRANSMISSION DENSITY WITH A MICROSYSTEM BY EXPLOITING PHOTONIC SIGNALING."]
